{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791594519,"nonce":"jITuJCx+nzd/V1GWtOfg/7C3V/k=","title":"Scrollbars: draw the thumb and add scroll helpers","message":"A scrolling box shows no indicator. native/src/scene.rs (set_scroll) and native/src/commands.rs (the SCROLL command) both pass thumb: [0.0; 4], so the thumb is never drawn (checked).\n\nScope\n- Carry a thumb colour in the scroll command and in set_scroll; the engine already draws the thumb (blinc_abi display_list.rs).\n- A thumb that appears while scrolling and fades, scrollbar visibility (auto, always, hover, hidden), and scroll limits and jump helpers; a scrollIntoView.\n- Native work is one colour in the scroll command; the fade timer is TypeScript and wants the frame scheduler from the motion issue (35f7bd0).\n\nReference, for structure: ashui's haxe/ashui/input/Scroll.hx.\n\nAcceptance: an overflowing box draws a thumb at the scroll position in offscreen pixels, the thumb moves with the scroll, and a hidden setting draws none.","files":null}]}